1. Permitted use and multi-tenant operation

Personal use, evaluation, modification, redistribution and single-tenant
self-hosting, including commercial single-tenant use, are permitted subject to
this license. Operating the Work or a derivative of the Work as a service or
platform for two or more independent tenants requires prior, explicit written
commercial authorization from the Licensor. This applies whether or not the
operator charges users, and whether tenancy is implemented in one deployment
or in separately deployed instances of the same offered service.

A tenant is an independently administered workspace or organization with its
own logically separated user access, data and configuration. Multiple users,
projects or devices within one such tenant do not by themselves constitute
multiple tenants. Giving the same service a different name does not avoid this
condition. Merely distributing source code does not constitute operating it.

Using the Nexus SDK, Mobile client, Computer Runtime or OpenWrt client solely
to connect to a service does not make the client user its multi-tenant operator.
The service operator remains responsible for authorization. An independent
application that only uses public interfaces, and does not operate the Work or
a derivative as a multi-tenant platform, is not restricted on that account.

2. Product attribution and branding

When operating or distributing a Nexus user interface or a derivative of it,
retain the Nexus names, logos, copyright notices and attribution displayed by
the supplied interface. Do not remove, replace, obscure or make them materially
less visible without prior written authorization from the Licensor. Additional
branding may be displayed without suggesting endorsement and without obscuring
the retained attribution. Ordinary responsive or accessibility adjustments that
preserve its meaning and visibility are permitted.

This applies to Nexus web consoles, Nexus-authored LuCI pages, Mobile screens
and other supplied graphical interfaces. It does not require an independent
interface or a headless SDK/API integration to add a Nexus logo it never
displayed. Source and redistribution notices must still be retained as required
by this license. No general trademark license or endorsement is granted.

