Contributions intended for incorporation must be covered by the separate Nexus
Contributor License Agreement, Version 1.0, or an individually executed written
agreement accepted by the Licensor. The contribution agreement provides the
rights needed for commercial use, dual licensing and future releases under
different, more permissive or more restrictive terms. Contributors retain
ownership. Mere use of the software is not acceptance of a contributor grant.

License changes apply to versions offered under the changed terms; they do not
revoke rights already granted for an earlier version. Existing contributions
are not deemed to have accepted a new contributor agreement retroactively.

